# ============================================================================
# KnowMemo — what must never reach a git remote
# ============================================================================
#
# The entries below fall into two groups, and they are not equally serious:
#
#   * **Personal data** — imported conversations, plaintext snapshots, the
#     metadata database. This is other people's words. A commit is not
#     recoverable by a later `git rm`: the object stays in the history and in
#     every clone, and on a public remote it must be assumed read.
#   * **Device and tooling noise** — caches, virtualenvs, editor droppings.
#
# `data/` is ignored as a whole rather than file by file because KnowMemo
# decides what goes in there at runtime, and a deny-list of filenames would
# always be one release behind.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- KnowMemo runtime data (design doc §42 Rule 8) ---------------------------
# data/raw, data/normalized, data/knowledge, data/logs and the metadata
# database all live here by default. Raw imported conversations must never be
# committed.
data/

# --- Databases, wherever they are -------------------------------------------
# `storage.database_url` is configurable, so the metadata database is not
# guaranteed to be under data/. The -wal sidecar matters on its own: it can
# hold messages that have not been checkpointed into the .db yet, so ignoring
# the database alone is not enough.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# --- Plaintext WeChat snapshots ---------------------------------------------
# The connector's input is a *directory* of SQLite files (docs/plan.md D4).
# These are the names people give them when they drop one beside the repo.
# NOTE: if you relocate `storage.database_url`, the derived tree moves with
# it — add that directory here too. KnowMemo writes conversations into
# <database parent>/normalized and <database parent>/knowledge.
snapshots/
snapshot/

# --- Local configuration and secrets ----------------------------------------
# knowmemo.yaml is a first-class config path (config/settings.py) and can hold
# `weknora.api_key` and absolute paths to your own machine.
knowmemo.yaml
knowmemo.local.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credentials, in the shapes they usually arrive in.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
.netrc

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheels/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Tooling caches ----------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- Scratch space -----------------------------------------------------------
# Test runs in restricted environments redirect tmp_path here. See README.
.tmp/
*.log
/logs/

# --- Assistant and editor workspace -----------------------------------------
# .workbuddy-ai/ holds the assistant's project memory: notes about this
# machine, paths outside the repo, and decisions taken in conversation. It is
# local context, not project source, and it is not written for an audience.
.workbuddy-ai/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- macOS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd

# --- Windows -----------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
